If a clinician conducts an MME-dosage-determination then it is recommended that the clinician does not include a buprenorphine in the MME-dosage-determination.
Every buprenorphine has a partial-opioid-receptor-agonist-property.
Every buprenorphine has a respiratory-depression-ceiling-effect.
If a buprenorphine has a partial-opioid-receptor-agonist-property and has a respiratory-depression-ceiling-effect then the partial-opioid-receptor-agonist-property causes the respiratory-depression-ceiling-effect.
